[2] (source: birthday_parties.md)
At AeroSports Scarborough, we offer three distinct birthday party packages: Premium, VIP, and Ultimate. Each package caters to groups of at least ten jumpers and includes a variety of amenities such as pizza, drinks, a private party room, a glow t-shirt, digital invitations, and a free sixty-minute add-on pass for guest jumpers.

The Premium Party is priced at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper. This package requires a minimum of ten jumpers with a base price of three hundred and ninety-nine dollars. It includes seventy-five minutes on the trampoline courts followed by forty-five minutes in a private party room, which accommodates twenty-five to thirty people. Food included consists of one large pizza for every five jumpers and one juice box per jumper. The birthday child receives a free glow t-shirt, digital invitations, and a free sixty-minute jump pass, while all guest jumpers get a free sixty-minute add-on pass. Go karting is not included but can be added on at nine dollars and ninety cents per person. There are no discounts for socks, no physical invitations provided, and bringing outside food incurs a fifty-dollar fee. The total party duration is approximately two hours.

The VIP Party costs forty-four dollars and ninety cents per jumper with the same minimum requirement of ten jumpers and a base price of four hundred and forty-nine dollars. This package offers ninety minutes on the trampoline courts followed by sixty minutes in a private party room, also accommodating twenty-five to thirty people. Food includes one large pizza for every five jumpers, plus one juice box and one water bottle per jumper. The birthday child receives a free glow t-shirt, digital invitations, and a free sixty-minute jump pass, while all guest jumpers receive a free sixty-minute add-on pass. Socks are available at fifty percent off, costing two dollars instead of three dollars and ninety-nine cents. Go karting can be added on for nine dollars and ninety cents per person, with no physical invitations included, and outside food requires a fifty-dollar fee. The total party duration is approximately two and a half hours.

The Ultimate Party is priced at fifty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper, also requiring a minimum of ten jumpers with a base price of five hundred and ninety-nine dollars. This package includes one hundred and twenty minutes on the trampoline courts followed by sixty minutes in a private party room for twenty-five to thirty people. Food consists of one large pizza for every five jumpers, plus one juice box or pop and one water bottle per jumper. The birthday child receives a free glow t-shirt, digital and physical invitations, and a free thirty-day jump pass. All guest jumpers receive a free sixty-minute add-on pass. Socks are provided for free to all jumpers, and go karting is included with one race per jumper. The fifty-dollar outside food fee is waived. The total party duration is approximately three hours.

When upgrading from the Premium Party to the VIP Party, you gain an additional fifteen minutes of jump time (ninety versus seventy-five), fifteen more minutes in the private room (sixty versus forty-five), a water bottle along with the juice box, and socks at fifty percent off (two dollars instead of three dollars and ninety-nine cents). The cost difference is five dollars per jumper, which amounts to fifty dollars for ten jumpers.

Upgrading from the VIP Party to the Ultimate Party adds thirty more minutes of jump time (one hundred and twenty versus ninety), includes go karting for every jumper, provides free socks for all jumpers, offers physical invitations, gives a birthday child a free thirty-day pass instead of sixty minutes, waives the fifty-dollar outside food fee, and allows drinks to include pop as an option. The cost difference is fifteen dollars per jumper, totaling one hundred and fifty dollars for ten jumpers.

The Ultimate Party offers the best value with go karting alone worth nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper (ninety-nine dollars for ten kids), free socks valued at three dollars and ninety-nine cents each (thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents for ten), and a waived fifty-dollar outside food fee. This equates to roughly one hundred and eighty-nine dollars in extras for one hundred and fifty dollars more than the VIP Party.

[3] (source: group_bookings.md)
At AeroSports Scarborough, we offer a variety of group booking options that cater to different needs and occasions. Whether you're planning a corporate event, school trip, fundraising activity, or simply want to enjoy some fun with friends or family, our packages are designed to accommodate groups effectively. Our offerings include discounts for larger groups, customizable packages for specific events, and exclusive facility rentals.

For general group bookings, we require a minimum of fifteen jumpers to qualify. If you have fifteen or more participants, you can use the discount code GROUPBOOKING25 to receive twenty-five percent off your booking. A deposit amounting to twenty-five percent is required at the time of booking. For groups opting for one hundred and twenty minutes of jump time, the price per jumper is twenty-five dollars and forty-seven cents after a twenty-five percent discount on the original rate of thirty-three dollars and eighty-nine cents. This discounted rate includes both jump time and Aero Socks, with additional options available at an extra cost. It's important to note that go-karting is not included in this group rate but can be added separately.

Corporate and team parties are perfect for team-building exercises, milestone celebrations, or employee rewards. We offer a lively environment featuring trampoline courts and obstacle courses among other activities. To arrange a corporate booking, you can call two-eight-nine-four-five-four-five-five-five-five or email events.scb@aerosportsparks.ca to discuss customizable packages tailored to your needs.

Schools, church groups, sports teams, and youth organizations are welcome for school and field trips at our facility. We require a minimum of fifteen participants and focus on promoting active play and teamwork in a safe environment. For booking information or inquiries about what's included, such as access to trampoline courts and obstacle courses, please call two-eight-nine-four-five-four-five-five-five-five or email events.scb@aerosportsparks.ca.

For fundraising events, AeroSports offers an opportunity for your organization to earn twenty percent of the night’s jump time sales. This option is ideal for schools, teams, troops, and community organizations looking to raise funds in a fun setting. To book a fundraiser with promotional support included, reach out by calling two-eight-nine-four-five-four-five-five-five-five or emailing events.scb@aerosportsparks.ca.

Our facility rentals provide exclusive access to the entire AeroSports Scarborough for either sixty minutes on weekdays (Monday through Thursday) at four thousand dollars or weekends (Friday through Sunday) at five thousand dollars. The capacity of our facility is up to two hundred and twenty jumpers, with private access and dedicated staff available on-site. Included in this rental are jump socks, all party rooms, and cutlery, though food and catering services come at an additional cost. Unlimited go-karting is also included with the facility rental.

For those interested in room rentals for parties or events, we offer several options: a Party Room (1, 2, 3, or 4) can be rented for one hundred dollars per forty-five minutes and accommodates twenty-five to thirty people. Alternatively, the Birds Eye Party Arena is available at two hundred dollars per forty-five minutes with a capacity of eighty people.

If you have any further questions or need assistance in planning your event, please don't hesitate to contact us. We're here to help make your experience at AeroSports Scarborough memorable and enjoyable!

[4] (source: voice_call_scripts.md)
Thank you for calling AeroSports Scarborough! How may I assist you today? We offer a variety of services including trampolines, go-karting, laser tag, and birthday party packages. Our offerings cater to different age groups and preferences, ensuring there's something exciting for everyone.

If you need some time while I retrieve information, please hold on one moment. Should your inquiry require more detailed assistance than I can provide, I will connect you with a team member who can help further. Thank you for calling AeroSports Scarborough! We look forward to seeing you and hope you have a wonderful day.

Our location is at 1120 Birchmount Road in Scarborough, with the postal code M1K 5G4. Please feel free to visit us anytime during our operating hours: Sunday through Thursday from ten ante meridiem to eight post meridiem, and Friday and Saturday from ten ante meridiem to ten post meridiem.

Regarding pricing, we offer a Premium Jump Pass for twenty-four dollars and ninety cents valid for ninety minutes. The VIP Jump Pass is priced at twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents for one hundred and twenty minutes. Additionally, there's an All Day Pass available for thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents, and the Ultimate Pass, which includes go-karting and laser tag among other activities, costs forty-nine dollars and ninety cents for one hundred and eighty minutes. Please note that all prices are plus tax. Aero Socks, required for trampoline activities, cost three dollars and ninety-nine cents but are reusable.

For birthday celebrations, we have three packages: the Premium Party starts at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper with seventy-five minutes of jump time and forty-five minutes in a private party room; the VIP Party is priced at forty-four dollars and ninety cents per jumper, offering ninety minutes of jump time and sixty minutes in the party room. The Ultimate Party costs fifty-nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper, providing one hundred and twenty minutes of jump time, sixty minutes in the party room, plus go-karting for every participant. All packages include pizza and drinks with a minimum requirement of ten jumpers.

Our go-karting tracks cater to different age groups: the main track is suitable for riders fifty-four inches or taller, costing nineteen dollars and ninety cents for a standalone race or nine dollars and ninety cents as an add-on if you have a jump pass. The mini track accommodates riders thirty-six inches or taller at nine dollars and ninety cents per standalone race or four dollars and ninety cents as an add-on. Each race allows up to ten laps, and remember, closed-toed shoes are required for safety.

To book your visit, you can do so online through our website aerosportsparks.ca, or I'd be happy to assist you with the booking process right now. Would you like to proceed?

A signed waiver is necessary for everyone entering the park, including non-jumpers. You can conveniently fill out this form online ahead of time at our website to save time during check-in. For participants under eighteen years old, a parent or legal guardian must sign the waiver.

For groups of fifteen or more, we offer a twenty-five percent discount with the code GROUPBOOKING25, reducing the price to approximately twenty-five dollars and forty-seven cents per person for one hundred and twenty minutes, including socks. Would you be interested in booking a group visit?

Currently, we have an April Birthday Promotion offering up to one hundred and fifty dollars off birthday parties. Use the code APRILBDAY50 for a discount of fifty dollars on a Premium party, APRILBDAY100 for one hundred dollars off a VIP party, or APRILBDAY150 for one hundred and fifty dollars off an Ultimate party. Please note that bookings must be made by April thirty-first and the event hosted by September thirtieth.

For children aged four to twelve years old, we offer AeroCamp with full-day sessions from eight-thirty ante meridiem to four-thirty post meridiem at sixty-nine dollars and ninety cents per day or two hundred and ninety-nine dollars and ninety cents for a full week. Half-day options are available for thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents. Activities include trampolines, games, challenges, crafts, and group activities. Early drop-off from seven-thirty ante meridiem and late pick-up past six post meridiem are available for ten dollars each.

[5] (source: birthday_parties.md)
Upgrading from the VIP Party to the Ultimate Party adds thirty more minutes of jump time (one hundred and twenty versus ninety), includes go karting for every jumper, provides free socks for all jumpers, offers physical invitations, gives a birthday child a free thirty-day pass instead of sixty minutes, waives the fifty-dollar outside food fee, and allows drinks to include pop as an option. The cost difference is fifteen dollars per jumper, totaling one hundred and fifty dollars for ten jumpers.

The Ultimate Party offers the best value with go karting alone worth nine dollars and ninety cents per jumper (ninety-nine dollars for ten kids), free socks valued at three dollars and ninety-nine cents each (thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents for ten), and a waived fifty-dollar outside food fee. This equates to roughly one hundred and eighty-nine dollars in extras for one hundred and fifty dollars more than the VIP Party.

Additional add-ons available include large pizzas—cheese, pepperoni, halal pepperoni, vegetarian, or Hawaiian—for twenty-five dollars each; juice boxes (ten boxes) for thirty dollars; soft drink cans (ten cans) for twenty dollars; physical birthday invitations at seventy-five cents each. An outside food fee of fifty dollars is waived for the Ultimate Party. Go kart races can be added on for nine dollars and ninety cents per person, already included in the Ultimate Party. A late ordering fee within twenty-four hours is twenty dollars.

The terms and conditions for booking a birthday party include free rescheduling up to one year from the booking date. Cancellations with fourteen or more days' notice receive a store gift card for the refund amount; cancellations within fourteen days receive no refund. Package changes must be made fourteen or more days in advance, subject to availability. Waivers are required for all jumpers (under eighteen must be signed by a parent/guardian and remain valid for one year). Room supplies such as plates, cups, and tablecloths are included. The jumping area is shared with other patrons, but the party room is private. Prohibited items include piñatas, confetti, or silly string, which incur a forty-dollar cleaning charge if used. Food allergies or sensitivities should be advised in advance. All guests should arrive twenty minutes early for check-in. AeroSports Scarborough is not responsible for lost or stolen items.

